% Tracheostomy Care Supplies: LCD L33832 and its Policy Article A52492 (DME
% MACs). A policy program of the DMEPOS model: it includes dmepos.le
% (orders, delivery, benefit category, continued need, refills) and states
% when a claim for a tracheostomy care supply — the starter kit (A4625), the
% care kit of an established tracheostomy (A4629), the tubes (A7520, A7521,
% A7522), the collar (A7526), the plug (A7527), the tracheostoma valve and
% the heat and moisture exchanger parts (A7501-A7509), the dressings, tape,
% swabs and the rest of the LCD's table (A4364, A4402, A4450, A4452, A4456,
% A4481, A4623, A4626, A5120, A7524) — is REASONABLE AND NECESSARY: the
% starter kit only in the first two weeks after an open surgical
% tracheostomy; every supply within the usual maximum quantity of the LCD's
% table, or beyond it with the greater quantity explained in the medical
% record; the tubes not for a beneficiary receiving a plug. A tracheostomy
% mask (A7523) is never covered ("a convenience item and therefore not
% covered"): no rule concludes it. The benefit is the prosthetic benefit
% (Policy Article A52492), which carries no condition on the place of use.
% The payment conditions the Article adds (section remedy): the supplies
% are for a beneficiary following an open surgical tracheostomy which has
% been open or is expected to remain open for at least three months; the
% diagnosis code that justifies the need, on each claim — a code of the
% Article's ICD-10 list (sources/icd10/A52492_icd10_covered.csv, one group,
% serving every code of the policy), loaded as the table trach_icd10; and
% the dispensing cap of the LCD's refill paragraph — a one-month supply at a
% time for a beneficiary in a nursing facility, three months at home.
%
% How the criteria are read. What the record states is a scenario fact: the
% date of the open surgical tracheostomy ("two weeks post-operatively" is
% 14 days, in the rule), that it is expected to be open for at least three
% months (the Article's "has been open or is expected to remain open": a
% tracheostomy open three months already is expected to be, a fortiori),
% the claim's diagnosis code, the residence. The quantities are the LCD's
% table, as data (the tables trach_quantity and trach_period, "# per Month
% (unless noted)"), read against the quantity billed and the months the
% claim supplies (the shared templates). One judgment is a finding, the
% judged template of dmepos.le "the finding F about B is established" (or
% unsupported), with who found it and why:
%   excess quantity of supplies explained (a quantity above the usual
%   maximum: "The explanation for use of a greater quantity of supplies than
%   the amounts listed must be clearly documented in the beneficiary's
%   medical record").
% That a beneficiary receives a plug (A7527) is derived from the items
% furnished to the beneficiary.
%
% Not modelled: the AU modifier of the tape and swabs and the Column II
% bundling of A4626 (billing and coding); the coding of the kits by the
% postoperative week (a kit billed as A4625 after two weeks is denied, the
% rule for A4625); the moisture exchanger of a ventilator (A4483) and the
% tracheostoma filter (A4481) beyond their quantities; the suction
% catheters, which the Suction Pumps policy decides.

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    % the record
    *a beneficiary* had an open surgical tracheostomy on *a date*; undefined.
    the tracheostomy of *a beneficiary* is expected to be open for at least three months; undefined.
    % the tables
    ICD10 code *a code* is in group *a group* of article *an article* as *a description* under table trach_icd10.
    the usual maximum for tracheostomy supply *a code* is *a quantity* under table trach_quantity.
    the period of the usual maximum for tracheostomy supply *a code* is *a number* months under table trach_period.
    % derived
    *an item* is a tracheostomy care supply other than the starter kit.
    *a beneficiary* receives a tracheostomy tube plug.
    *an item* is a tracheostomy tube excluded by a plug.
    *a claim* is within the usual maximum quantity of tracheostomy supplies.
    *a claim* is within the listed amount of tracheostomy supplies.
    the quantity of *a claim* is allowed for *a beneficiary*.
    *a beneficiary* has a qualifying open surgical tracheostomy.
    the diagnosis code of *a beneficiary* is a covered tracheostomy diagnosis code.
    *a claim* is within the dispensing limit for tracheostomy supplies.

% The Policy Article's ICD-10 table: the covered codes of its one group.
the table trach_icd10 is loaded from sources/icd10/A52492_icd10_covered.csv, with all matches:
    code | group | article | description

% The usual maximum quantity of each supply, and the months it is per (LCD
% L33832, "USUAL MAXIMUM QUANTITY OF SUPPLIES"): per month unless noted.
the table trach_quantity is, with unique match, with provenance LCD L33832,
        confer "The table below lists the maximum number of items/units of service that are usually reasonable and necessary":
    code    | quantity | confer
    "A4364" | 4        | "A4364 4"
    "A4402" | 4        | "A4402 4"
    "A4450" | 40       | "A4450 40"
    "A4452" | 40       | "A4452 40"
    "A4456" | 50       | "A4456 50"
    "A4481" | 62       | "A4481 62"
    "A4623" | 62       | "A4623 62"
    "A4625" | 31       | "A4625 31"
    "A4626" | 2        | "A4626 2"
    "A4629" | 31       | "A4629 31"
    "A5120" | 150      | "A5120 150"
    "A7501" | 1        | "A7501 1"
    "A7502" | 1        | "A7502 1"
    "A7503" | 1        | "A7503 1 per 6 months"
    "A7504" | 62       | "A7504 62"
    "A7505" | 2        | "A7505 2 per 3 months"
    "A7506" | 62       | "A7506 62"
    "A7507" | 62       | "A7507 62"
    "A7508" | 62       | "A7508 62"
    "A7509" | 62       | "A7509 62"
    "A7520" | 1        | "A7520 1 per 3 months"
    "A7521" | 1        | "A7521 1 per 3 months"
    "A7522" | 1        | "A7522 1 per 12 months"
    "A7524" | 1        | "A7524 1 per 3 months"
    "A7526" | 31       | "A7526 31"
    "A7527" | 2        | "A7527 2 per 3 months"

the table trach_period is, with unique match, with provenance LCD L33832,
        confer "The table below lists the maximum number of items/units of service that are usually reasonable and necessary":
    code    | months | confer
    "A4364" | 1      | "A4364 4"
    "A4402" | 1      | "A4402 4"
    "A4450" | 1      | "A4450 40"
    "A4452" | 1      | "A4452 40"
    "A4456" | 1      | "A4456 50"
    "A4481" | 1      | "A4481 62"
    "A4623" | 1      | "A4623 62"
    "A4625" | 1      | "A4625 31"
    "A4626" | 1      | "A4626 2"
    "A4629" | 1      | "A4629 31"
    "A5120" | 1      | "A5120 150"
    "A7501" | 1      | "A7501 1"
    "A7502" | 1      | "A7502 1"
    "A7503" | 6      | "A7503 1 per 6 months"
    "A7504" | 1      | "A7504 62"
    "A7505" | 3      | "A7505 2 per 3 months"
    "A7506" | 1      | "A7506 62"
    "A7507" | 1      | "A7507 62"
    "A7508" | 1      | "A7508 62"
    "A7509" | 1      | "A7509 62"
    "A7520" | 3      | "A7520 1 per 3 months"
    "A7521" | 3      | "A7521 1 per 3 months"
    "A7522" | 12     | "A7522 1 per 12 months"
    "A7524" | 3      | "A7524 1 per 3 months"
    "A7526" | 1      | "A7526 31"
    "A7527" | 3      | "A7527 2 per 3 months"

the knowledge base tracheostomy_supplies includes these resources:
    dmepos.

the knowledge base tracheostomy_supplies includes:

LCD L33832 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/lcd.aspx?lcdid=33832".
the text of LCD L33832 is at "sources/lcd/L33832.txt".
Policy Article A52492 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/article.aspx?articleid=52492".
the text of Policy Article A52492 is at "sources/article/A52492.txt".

% The supplies of the LCD's table other than the starter kit, which has its
% own rule.
rule trach_supply with provenance LCD L33832,
        confer "The table below lists the maximum number of items/units of service that are usually reasonable and necessary":
an item is a tracheostomy care supply other than the starter kit
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["A4364", "A4402", "A4450", "A4452", "A4456", "A4481", "A4623", "A4626", "A4629", "A5120", "A7501", "A7502", "A7503", "A7504", "A7505", "A7506", "A7507", "A7508", "A7509", "A7520", "A7521", "A7522", "A7524", "A7526", "A7527"].

% A plug is an alternative to a tube: the tubes of a beneficiary receiving
% a plug are denied.
rule trach_plug with provenance LCD L33832,
        confer "A7527 (Tracheostomy/laryngectomy tube plug/stop) is used as an alternative to a tracheostomy/laryngectomy tube":
a beneficiary receives a tracheostomy tube plug
    if an item is furnished to the beneficiary
    and the HCPCS code of the item is "A7527".

rule trach_tube_excluded with provenance LCD L33832,
        confer "for a beneficiary receiving A7527 claims for A7520, A7521 and A7522 will be denied as not reasonable or necessary":
an item is a tracheostomy tube excluded by a plug
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["A7520", "A7521", "A7522"]
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary receives a tracheostomy tube plug.

% The codes this policy decides — outside the section checklist: a claim
% of another policy fails here without failing its own applicability.
% The codes this policy decides: the supplies of the LCD's table and the
% mask it denies; their benefit: the prosthetic benefit (Policy Article
% A52492), with no condition on the place of use.
rule trach_codes with provenance Policy Article A52492,
        confer "Tracheostomy Supplies are covered under the Prosthetic Benefit":
the policy for code a code is tracheostomy_supplies
    if the code is in ["A4364", "A4402", "A4450", "A4452", "A4456", "A4481", "A4623", "A4625", "A4626", "A4629", "A5120", "A7501", "A7502", "A7503", "A7504", "A7505", "A7506", "A7507", "A7508", "A7509", "A7520", "A7521", "A7522", "A7523", "A7524", "A7526", "A7527"].

section applicability is:

rule trach_benefit with provenance Policy Article A52492,
        confer "Tracheostomy Supplies are covered under the Prosthetic Benefit":
the benefit category of code a code is prosthetic devices
    if the policy for code the code is tracheostomy_supplies.

section question is:

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The starter kit: the first two weeks after the tracheostomy. The other
% supplies: within the usual quantities, and no tube beside a plug. The
% mask (A7523) has no rule: "A7523 is a convenience item and therefore not
% covered. Claims for A7523 will be denied as not reasonable and necessary."
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule trach_starter_kit with provenance LCD L33832,
        confer "A tracheostomy care or cleaning starter kit (A4625) is covered following an open surgical tracheostomy":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is "A4625"
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary had an open surgical tracheostomy on a date
    and the date of service of the claim is an other date
    and the other date is a number days after the date
    and the number >= 0
    and the number < 14
    and the claim is within the usual maximum quantity of tracheostomy supplies.

% "Beginning two weeks post-operatively, code A4625 is no longer medically
% necessary and, if that code is billed, will be denied as not reasonable
% and necessary": two weeks are 14 days, the bound of the rule above.

rule trach_supplies_covered with provenance LCD L33832,
        confer "The actual quantity needed for a particular beneficiary may be more or less than the amount listed depending on clinical factors that affect the frequency of supply changes":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is a tracheostomy care supply other than the starter kit
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the claim is within the usual maximum quantity of tracheostomy supplies
    and it is not the case that
        the item is a tracheostomy tube excluded by a plug.

% The usual maximum: the table's quantity per its period, over the months
% the claim supplies; a greater quantity only when the medical record
% explains it (the finding) — asked only once the usual maximum is exceeded.
rule trach_usual_quantity with provenance LCD L33832,
        confer "The explanation for use of a greater quantity of supplies than the amounts listed must be clearly documented in the beneficiary’s medical record":
a claim is within the usual maximum quantity of tracheostomy supplies
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the quantity of the claim is allowed for the beneficiary.

% the cascade decides one claim and one beneficiary at a time (both bound
% by the head): within the listed amount, otherwise the explanation
rule trach_quantity_allowed with provenance LCD L33832,
        confer "The explanation for use of a greater quantity of supplies than the amounts listed must be clearly documented in the beneficiary’s medical record":
the quantity of a claim is allowed for a beneficiary
    if the claim is within the listed amount of tracheostomy supplies
    otherwise the finding excess quantity of supplies explained about the beneficiary is established.

rule trach_listed_amount with provenance LCD L33832,
        confer "If adequate documentation is not provided when requested, the excess quantities will be denied as not reasonable and necessary":
a claim is within the listed amount of tracheostomy supplies
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the usual maximum for tracheostomy supply the code is a quantity under table trach_quantity
    and the period of the usual maximum for tracheostomy supply the code is a number months under table trach_period
    and the claim is for a supply of an other number months
    and the quantity billed on the claim is a third number
    and a limit is the quantity * ceiling(the other number / the number)
    and the third number <= the limit.

section remedy is:

% The Policy Article's own conditions of payment: the open surgical
% tracheostomy open or expected to remain open for three months, the
% diagnosis code on the claim, and the dispensing cap of the LCD's refill
% paragraph.
rule trach_documentation with provenance Policy Article A52492,
        confer "In addition, there are specific statutory payment policy requirements, discussed below, that also must be met":
the policy specific documentation requirements are met for a claim
    if the policy of the claim is tracheostomy_supplies
    and the claim is for an item
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary has a qualifying open surgical tracheostomy
    and the diagnosis code of the beneficiary is a covered tracheostomy diagnosis code
    and the claim is within the dispensing limit for tracheostomy supplies.

rule trach_statutory_tracheostomy with provenance Policy Article A52492,
        confer "Supplies for care of a tracheostomy site are covered for a beneficiary following an open surgical tracheostomy which has been open or is expected to remain open for at least three months":
a beneficiary has a qualifying open surgical tracheostomy
    if the beneficiary had an open surgical tracheostomy on a date
    and the tracheostomy of the beneficiary is expected to be open for at least three months.

rule trach_diagnosis_code with provenance Policy Article A52492,
        confer "The diagnosis code that justifies the need for these items must be included on each claim":
the diagnosis code of a beneficiary is a covered tracheostomy diagnosis code
    if the diagnosis code of the beneficiary is a code
    and ICD10 code the code is in group 1 of article "A52492" as a description under table trach_icd10.

rule trach_dispensing_nursing_facility with provenance LCD L33832,
        confer "a supplier must not dispense more than a 1-month supply at a time for a beneficiary in a nursing facility and a 3-month supply for a beneficiary at home":
a claim is within the dispensing limit for tracheostomy supplies
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the residence of the beneficiary is nursing facility
    and the claim is for a supply of a number months
    and the number <= 1.

rule trach_dispensing_home with provenance LCD L33832,
        confer "a supplier must not dispense more than a 1-month supply at a time for a beneficiary in a nursing facility and a 3-month supply for a beneficiary at home":
a claim is within the dispensing limit for tracheostomy supplies
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and it is not the case that
        the residence of the beneficiary is nursing facility
    and the claim is for a supply of a number months
    and the number <= 3.
